========================================================================
Standards, Specifications & Technical References
========================================================================

Craftpack implements, conforms to, and references specifications established
by the open-source community:

* Debian Policy Manual & Packaging Standards
  https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/
  Specifications for Debian package structure, FHS filesystem layout,
  ELF binary hardening (Position Independent Executables), stripped symbol
  tables, maintainer script hooks, conffiles, and md5sums.

* Debian Machine-Readable Copyright Format (DEP-5)
  https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
  Specification for machine-readable copyright files conforming to DEP-5.

* Debian Changelog Specification
  https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/ch-source.html#s-dpkgchangelog
  Format for Debian package changelogs and RFC 5322 date formatting.

* Reproducible Builds & SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH Specification
  https://reproducible-builds.org/specs/source-date-epoch/
  Standard for bit-for-bit reproducible packaging archives and deterministic
  timestamp normalization.

* Software Package Data Exchange (SPDX) Specification
  https://spdx.dev/
  Standard machine-readable license expression syntax and identifier list
  maintained by the Linux Foundation.

* REUSE Specification 3.3
  https://reuse.software/
  Best practices for declaring machine-readable copyright and licensing
  information developed by the Free Software Foundation Europe (FSFE).

* Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 (SemVer)
  https://semver.org/
  Specification for software release versioning and API compatibility semantics.

========================================================================
Development, Testing & Verification References
========================================================================

The following open-source tools and infrastructure are utilized within the
development, verification, and testing pipelines of Craftpack:

* Lintian (Debian Package Checker)
  https://wiki.debian.org/Lintian
  Upstream Debian Policy compliance verification tool used in automated
  integration tests to validate package conformance.

* FSFE REUSE Tool
  https://github.com/fsfe/reuse-tool
  Automated compliance linter for the REUSE 3.3 specification.

* Debian Container Images (Debian Project)
  https://hub.docker.com/_/debian
  Official Debian distribution container images used for automated
  containerized installation and execution smoke testing.
